──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
psycopg's LGPL — what it means in practice
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

psycopg (used by the [postgres] extra to power the wizard's
saved-ontologies store on Postgres) is distributed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License v3.0.  Apache-2.0 and LGPL-3.0 are
compatible for the case where psycopg is *used as a library*
(linked dynamically via Python imports) without modification, as
this project does.

If you redistribute Ontomesh together with a modified copy of
psycopg, those modifications must remain under LGPL-3.0.  If you
redistribute Ontomesh without psycopg (e.g. by using the SQLite
backend only), the LGPL has no further effect.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The drift-monitor (`infodrift`) dependency
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The optional [drift] extra installs `drift-monitor` from a separate
git repository (https://github.com/synaptixs/infodrift).
At the time of writing that repository is private; the license
applies whatever terms are documented in that repository when it
becomes accessible.  The [drift] extra is opt-in; the core toolkit
does not require it.

